.TH tuprovider-dav n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuprovider::dav
.PP
A WebDAV backend for the \fBtuprovider\fR interface, built on \fBtudav\fR.
.PP
It lets the same tree and list consumers that work over the local filesystem work over a WebDAV server without change: for the consumer, a DAV path is just a path with children.
.SS Load
.CS
tcl::tm::path add /path/to/tclutils/lib/tm
package require tclutils::tuprovider::dav
.CE
.PP
Loading the package registers the \fBdav\fR scheme with \fBtuprovider\fR.
.SS Open
.CS
set p [::tclutils::tuprovider open dav https://host/remote.php/dav/files/me/]
.CE
.PP
Extra arguments after the URL are passed through to \fBtudav::client\fR (for credentials and options).
.SS Capabilities
.PP
\fBdav\fR reports:
.CS
list stat get put delete
.CE
.PP
It deliberately does \fBnot\fR report \fBmkdir\fR, \fBmove\fR or \fBcopy\fR: \fBtudav\fR has no public MKCOL/MOVE/COPY, so the provider reports honestly what it can do. A UI driven by \fBcaps\fR will not offer operations that would fail.
.SS Operations
.IP \(bu
\fBlist $path\fR \-\- returns entry dicts for the collections and resources under \fB$path\fR. Collections become \fBtype dir\fR, resources \fBtype file\fR. The entry \fBname\fR is derived from the href tail (\fB/a/b/\fR \-> \fBb\fR, \fB/a/f.txt\fR \-> \fBf.txt\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fBstat $path\fR \-\- a cheap existence/type check via a depth\-0 request.
.IP \(bu
\fBget $path\fR \-\- fetches the resource bytes.
.IP \(bu
\fBput $path $bytes\fR, \fBdelete $path\fR \-\- the writing half.
.SS "Notes and limits"
.IP \(bu
Paths are DAV hrefs, relative to the client URL; the consumer treats them as opaque paths.
.IP \(bu
\fBstat\fR derives dir/file heuristically from a trailing slash, because \fBtudav\fR's property lookup does not report the type reliably across servers.
.IP \(bu
\fBname\fR derivation keeps percent\-decoding minimal; hrefs are usually clean.
.IP \(bu
The HTTP traffic itself is \fBtudav\fR's concern. What this adapter adds is the href \-> entry mapping and the honest \fBcaps\fR subset.
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtuprovider\fR, \fBtuprovider::zip\fR, \fBtudav\fR
